IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 4 Division 8, ss 134 to 138: the Registrar's register of charges, the notice and the certificate, the endorsement on debentures,
-- the entries of satisfaction and release, the Court's extension of time and rectification, and the company's copies and register.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. The Registrar and the Court appear only as what their acts mean to the person (a duty owed to the company, a power the person can invoke).
-- Marks in the comments: "FALSE-kind" and "NOTHING-kind" say why a branch answers JUST FALSE or NOTHING; "fork F-Kn" points at the fork register of NOTES.md.

§ `The nouns of ss 134 to 138`

DECLARE `s 134 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 134(1) enter the particulars of the charge in the register`
    `s 134(2) issue to the company a notice of the registration of the charge`
    `s 134(3) issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge`
    `s 135(1) endorse on the debenture or certificate of debenture stock a copy of the notice of registration or a statement of the registration`
    `s 135(3) authorise or permit the delivery of a debenture or certificate of debenture stock not endorsed as section 135 requires`
    `s 136(1) enter the particulars of the statement of satisfaction or release in the register`
    `s 138(1) keep the instrument creating the charge, or a copy, at the registered office`
    `s 138(1) cease to keep the instrument creating the charge, or a copy, at the registered office while the charge remains in force`
    `s 138(2) keep a register of charges at the registered office`
    `s 138(3A) furnish the person with a copy of an instrument or debenture kept under section 138`

DECLARE `s 134(1) kind of charge` IS ONE OF
    `s 134(1)(a) a charge to the benefit of which the holders of a series of debentures are entitled`
    `s 134(1)(b) any other charge created by the company`
    `s 134(1)(b) any other charge existing on property acquired by the company`

DECLARE `s 137 order` IS ONE OF
    `s 137 an order that the time for registration be extended`
    `s 137 an order that the omission or mis-statement be rectified`

DECLARE `s 138(3) who asks to inspect` IS ONE OF
    `s 138(3) a creditor of the company`
    `s 138(3) a member of the company`
    `s 138(3) any other person`

DECLARE `s 138(3) what is to be inspected` IS ONE OF
    `s 138(3) the instruments or copies kept under section 138`
    `s 138(3) the register of charges`

§ `Section 134(1): what the Registrar enters in the register`

-- src:11297 | 134.—(1) The Registrar must keep a register of all the charges
-- src:11298 | lodged for registration under this Division and must enter in the
-- src:11299 | register with respect to those charges the following particulars:
-- src:11301 | (a) in the case of a charge to the benefit of which the holders of
-- src:11302 | a series of debentures are entitled — such particulars as are
-- src:11303 | required to be contained in a statement furnished under
-- src:11304 | section 131(5);
-- src:11306 | (b) in the case of any other charge —
-- src:11308 | (i) if the charge is a charge created by the company, the
-- src:11309 | date of its creation, and if the charge was a charge
-- src:11310 | existing on property acquired by the company the
-- src:11311 | date of the acquisition of the property;
-- src:11313 | (ii) the amount secured by the charge;
-- src:11315 | (iii) a description sufficient to identify the property
-- src:11316 | charged; and
-- src:11318 | (iv) the name of the person entitled to the charge.
@ref s 134(1) (src:11297-11318)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 134(1) kind of charge`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 134(1) the particulars the Registrar must enter in the register` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 134(1)(a) a charge to the benefit of which the holders of a series of debentures are entitled` THEN
        LIST "the total amount secured by the whole series",
             "the dates of the resolutions authorising the issue of the series and the date of the covering instrument (if any) by which the security is created or defined",
             "a general description of the property charged",
             "the names of the trustee (if any) for the debenture holders"
    WHEN `s 134(1)(b) any other charge created by the company` THEN
        LIST "the date of the creation of the charge",
             "the amount secured by the charge",
             "a description sufficient to identify the property charged",
             "the name of the person entitled to the charge"
    WHEN `s 134(1)(b) any other charge existing on property acquired by the company` THEN
        LIST "the date of the acquisition of the property",
             "the amount secured by the charge",
             "a description sufficient to identify the property charged",
             "the name of the person entitled to the charge"

-- The duty as a regulative rule. It has no time limit and the text states no consequence, so no trace can show it breached (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 134(1) (src:11297-11318)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 134 act`
`s 134(1) the Registrar must enter the particulars of the charge in the register` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 134(1) enter the particulars of the charge in the register`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 134(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not enter the particulars of a charge lodged for registration in the register" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

§ `Section 134(2) and (3): the notice and the certificate`

-- src:11320 | (2) The Registrar must issue a notice to the company concerned of
-- src:11321 | the registration of a charge and the notice is conclusive evidence that
-- src:11322 | the requirements as to registration have been complied with.
@ref s 134(2) (src:11320-11322)
GIVEN `the Registrar has issued to the company a notice of the registration of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(2) the notice is conclusive evidence that the requirements as to registration have been complied with` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has issued to the company a notice of the registration of the charge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence makes "the notice" conclusive evidence; where no notice has been issued it says nothing of the requirements as to registration

@ref s 134(2) (src:11320-11322)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 134 act`
`s 134(2) the Registrar must issue to the company a notice of the registration of a charge` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 134(2) issue to the company a notice of the registration of the charge`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 134(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not issue to the company a notice of the registration of the charge" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:11324 | (3) Upon the application of the company and payment of the
-- src:11325 | prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate
-- src:11326 | confirming the registration of the charge and the certificate is
-- src:11327 | conclusive evidence that the requirements as to registration have been
-- src:11328 | complied with.
@ref s 134(3) (src:11324-11328)
GIVEN `the company has applied for a certificate confirming the registration of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has paid the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(3) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge` MEANS
    IF `the company has applied for a certificate confirming the registration of the charge` AND `the company has paid the prescribed fee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty arises "Upon the application of the company and payment of the prescribed fee"; an "upon" unmet on a duty (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork F-K5)

@ref s 134(3) (src:11324-11328)
GIVEN `the Registrar has issued the certificate to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(3) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the requirements as to registration have been complied with` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has issued the certificate to the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence makes "the certificate" conclusive evidence; where none has been issued it says nothing of the requirements as to registration

@ref s 134(3) (src:11324-11328)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 134 act`
`s 134(3) the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 134(3) issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 134(3) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not issue the certificate to the company on its application and payment of the prescribed fee" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

§ `Section 135: endorsement on debentures`

-- src:11335 | 135.—(1) The company must cause to be endorsed on every
-- src:11336 | debenture forming one of a series of debentures, or certificate of
-- src:11337 | debenture stock which is issued by the company and the payment of
-- src:11338 | which is secured by a charge so registered —
-- src:11340 | (a) a copy of the notice of registration; or
-- src:11342 | (b) a statement that the registration has been effected and the
-- src:11343 | date of registration.
-- src:11345 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to any debenture or certificate of
-- src:11346 | debenture stock which has been issued by the company before the
-- src:11347 | charge was registered.
-- src:11349 | (3) Every person who knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits
-- src:11350 | the delivery of any debenture or certificate of debenture stock which
-- src:11351 | is not endorsed as required by this section shall be guilty of an offence
-- src:11352 | and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000.
@ref s 135 (src:11335-11352)
GIVEN `the debenture forms one of a series of debentures, or is a certificate of debenture stock, issued by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `payment of the debenture or certificate is secured by a charge registered under Division 8` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debenture or certificate was issued by the company before the charge was registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135(1) the company must cause a copy of the notice of registration, or a statement of the registration and its date, to be endorsed on the debenture or certificate` MEANS
    IF `the debenture or certificate was issued by the company before the charge was registered`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to any debenture or certificate of debenture stock which has been issued by the company before the charge was registered" (s 135(2))
    ELSE (IF `the debenture forms one of a series of debentures, or is a certificate of debenture stock, issued by the company` AND `payment of the debenture or certificate is secured by a charge registered under Division 8`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is stated for "every debenture forming one of a series of debentures, or certificate of debenture stock which is issued by the company and the payment of which is secured by a charge so registered"; the section says nothing of any other instrument (a scope limit with no "only": periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

-- The duty as a regulative rule. It has no time limit; the offence of s 135(3) is for authorising delivery of an unendorsed instrument, not for the omission itself (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 135(1) (src:11335-11343)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 134 act`
`s 135(1) the company must cause the endorsement to be made` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 135(1) endorse on the debenture or certificate of debenture stock a copy of the notice of registration or a statement of the registration`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 135(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the debenture or certificate of debenture stock was not endorsed with the notice of registration or a statement of the registration" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

@ref s 135(3) (src:11349-11352)
GIVEN `the person knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the delivery of the debenture or certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debenture or certificate is not endorsed as section 135 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 135(3) the person is guilty of the offence of authorising or permitting the delivery of an unendorsed debenture or certificate` MEANS
    IF `the person knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the delivery of the debenture or certificate` AND `the debenture or certificate is not endorsed as section 135 requires`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): an element of the offence is unmet ("Every person who knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the delivery of any debenture or certificate of debenture stock which is not endorsed as required by this section shall be guilty of an offence"); split site (i); fork F-K10

@ref s 135(3) (src:11349-11352)
GIVEN `the person knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the delivery of the debenture or certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debenture or certificate is not endorsed as section 135 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 135(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits the delivery of the debenture or certificate` AND `the debenture or certificate is not endorsed as section 135 requires`
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 2000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000"; no imprisonment and no default penalty
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is fixed only for a person the subsection makes guilty

-- The offence as a prohibition (derived from the offence, N2 of 2026-11-04): the person is any person who authorises or permits the delivery.
@ref s 135(3) (src:11349-11352)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 134 act`
`s 135(3) a person must not knowingly and wilfully authorise or permit the delivery of an unendorsed debenture or certificate` MEANS   -- fork F-K34: a prohibition derived from the offence of s 135(3); the text names the bearer ("Every person who knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits")
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    SHANT `s 135(3) authorise or permit the delivery of a debenture or certificate of debenture stock not endorsed as section 135 requires`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the person knowingly and wilfully authorised or permitted the delivery of a debenture or certificate of debenture stock not endorsed as section 135 requires"

§ `Section 136: entries of satisfaction and release`

-- src:11356 | 136.—(1) Where, with respect to any registered charge —
-- src:11358 | (a) the debt for which the charge was given has been paid or
-- src:11359 | satisfied in whole or in part; or
-- src:11361 | (b) the property or undertaking charged or any part thereof has
-- src:11362 | been released from the charge or has ceased to form part of
-- src:11363 | the company’s property or undertaking of the company
-- src:11364 | concerned,
-- src:11366 | the company may lodge with the Registrar in the prescribed form a
-- src:11367 | statement of satisfaction in whole or in part, or of the fact that the
-- src:11368 | property or undertaking or any part thereof has been released from the
-- src:11369 | charge or has ceased to form part of the company’s property or
-- src:11370 | undertaking (as the case may be) and the Registrar must enter
-- src:11371 | particulars of that statement in the register.
@ref s 136(1) (src:11356-11371)
GIVEN `the debt for which the registered charge was given has been paid or satisfied in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property or undertaking charged, or any part of it, has been released from the charge or has ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(1) the company may lodge with the Registrar a statement of satisfaction or release` MEANS
    IF `the debt for which the registered charge was given has been paid or satisfied in whole or in part` OR `the property or undertaking charged, or any part of it, has been released from the charge or has ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection begins "Where, with respect to any registered charge — (a) the debt ... has been paid or satisfied ...; or (b) the property ... has been released"; a "may" gated by "where" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-K7)

@ref s 136(1) (src:11356-11371)
GIVEN `the company has lodged a statement of satisfaction or release with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(1) the Registrar must enter the particulars of the statement in the register` MEANS
    IF `the company has lodged a statement of satisfaction or release with the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty follows the lodging of the statement ("the company may lodge ... a statement ... and the Registrar must enter particulars of that statement"); with no statement lodged there is nothing to enter (fork F-K5)

@ref s 136(1) (src:11356-11371)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 134 act`
`s 136(1) the Registrar must enter the particulars of the statement in the register` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 136(1) enter the particulars of the statement of satisfaction or release in the register`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 136(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not enter the particulars of the statement of satisfaction or release in the register" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:11373 | (2) The statement must be endorsed with a statement by the chargee
-- src:11374 | of the payment, satisfaction, release or ceasing referred to in
-- src:11375 | subsection (1) (as the case may be) and the second‑mentioned
-- src:11380 | statement constitutes sufficient evidence of that payment,
-- src:11381 | satisfaction, release or ceasing.
@ref s 136(2) (src:11373-11381)
GIVEN `the statement is endorsed with a statement by the chargee of the payment, satisfaction, release or ceasing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(2) the statement of satisfaction or release is endorsed as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the statement is endorsed with a statement by the chargee of the payment, satisfaction, release or ceasing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement must be endorsed with a statement by the chargee"; a duty not met, the provision's own question

@ref s 136(2) (src:11373-11381)
GIVEN `the statement is endorsed with a statement by the chargee of the payment, satisfaction, release or ceasing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136(2) the chargee's statement constitutes sufficient evidence of the payment, satisfaction, release or ceasing` MEANS
    IF `the statement is endorsed with a statement by the chargee of the payment, satisfaction, release or ceasing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence makes "the second-mentioned statement", the chargee's, sufficient evidence; it says nothing of other proof

§ `Section 137: extension of time and rectification of the register`

-- src:11385 | 137. The Court, on being satisfied that the omission to register a
-- src:11386 | charge (whether under this or any corresponding previous written
-- src:11387 | law) within the time required or that the omission or mis‑statement of
-- src:11388 | any particular with respect to any such charge or in a statement of
-- src:11389 | satisfaction was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other
-- src:11390 | sufficient cause or is not of a nature to prejudice the position of
-- src:11391 | creditors or shareholders or that on other grounds it is just and
-- src:11392 | equitable to grant relief, may on the application of the company or
-- src:11393 | any person interested and on such terms and conditions as seem to the
-- src:11394 | Court just and expedient (including a term or condition that the
-- src:11395 | extension or rectification is to be without prejudice to any liability
-- src:11396 | already incurred by the company or any of its officers in respect of the
-- src:11397 | default) order that the time for registration be extended or that the
-- src:11398 | omission or mis‑statement be rectified.
@ref s 137 (src:11385-11398)
GIVEN `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person interested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge was not registered within the time required, or a particular was omitted or mis-stated in the register of charges or in a statement of satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137 the person may apply to the Court for the extension of time or the rectification` MEANS
    IF (`the person is the company` OR `the person is a person interested`) AND `the charge was not registered within the time required, or a particular was omitted or mis-stated in the register of charges or in a statement of satisfaction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section names an application "of the company or any person interested" for an omission or mis-statement of the kind it describes; it says nothing of another applicant or another defect

@ref s 137 (src:11385-11398)
GIVEN `an application is made by the company or a person interested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the omission or mis-statement was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the omission or mis-statement is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137 the Court may order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` MEANS
    IF `an application is made by the company or a person interested`
       AND (   `the Court is satisfied that the omission or mis-statement was accidental or due to inadvertence or to some other sufficient cause`
            OR `the Court is satisfied that the omission or mis-statement is not of a nature to prejudice the position of creditors or shareholders`
            OR `the Court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Court's power is stated "on being satisfied" and "on the application of the company or any person interested"; the section does not say the Court may not act otherwise (fork F-K13, split site (ii): "on application" and "on being satisfied", not "where", "when" or "upon")

@ref s 137 (src:11385-11398)
GIVEN `the Court grants relief under section 137` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137 the Court may make the relief subject to a term that it is without prejudice to liability already incurred in respect of the default` MEANS
    IF `the Court grants relief under section 137`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the term is one of "such terms and conditions as seem to the Court just and expedient" on which the Court orders relief; where it grants none the section is silent

§ `Section 138: the company's copies and register`

-- src:11403 | 138.—(1) Every company must cause the instrument creating any
-- src:11404 | charge requiring registration under this Division or a copy thereof to
-- src:11405 | be kept at the registered office of the company for as long as the
-- src:11406 | charge to which the instrument relates remains in force, but in the
-- src:11407 | case of a series of debentures the keeping of a copy of one debenture
-- src:11408 | of the series is sufficient for the purposes of this subsection.
@ref s 138(1) (src:11403-11408)
GIVEN `the charge requires registration under Division 8` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge remains in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(1) the company must keep the instrument creating the charge, or a copy, at its registered office` MEANS
    IF NOT `the charge requires registration under Division 8`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is stated for "any charge requiring registration under this Division"; the subsection says nothing of another charge
    ELSE (IF `the charge remains in force`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the instrument is to be kept "for as long as the charge to which the instrument relates remains in force"; the period has ended (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

@ref s 138(1) (src:11403-11408)
GIVEN `the company keeps the instrument creating the charge, or a copy, at its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is one of a series of debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company keeps a copy of one debenture of the series at its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(1) the company's keeping satisfies the subsection` MEANS
    IF `the company keeps the instrument creating the charge, or a copy, at its registered office`
       OR (`the charge is one of a series of debentures` AND `the company keeps a copy of one debenture of the series at its registered office`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every company must cause the instrument ... or a copy thereof to be kept at the registered office ... but in the case of a series of debentures the keeping of a copy of one debenture of the series is sufficient"; a duty not met, the provision's own question

-- The duty as a regulative rule, as the text words it: a MUST with no time limit, so no trace can show it breached (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 138(1) (src:11403-11408)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 134 act`
`s 138(1) the company must keep the instrument or a copy at its registered office` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 138(1) keep the instrument creating the charge, or a copy, at the registered office`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 138(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not keep the instrument creating a charge requiring registration, or a copy, at its registered office" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- The same duty as a prohibition for as long as the charge remains in force (derived from the duty; fork F-K16): ceasing to keep the instrument while the charge is in force is the breach.
-- SHANT ... WITHIN n sunsets at n, which is the charge's life: the number of days the charge remains in force.
@ref s 138(1) (src:11403-11408)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days the charge remains in force` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 134 act`
`s 138(1) the company must not cease to keep the instrument or a copy at its registered office while the charge remains in force` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 138(1) cease to keep the instrument creating the charge, or a copy, at the registered office while the charge remains in force`
    WITHIN `the number of days the charge remains in force`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company ceased to keep the instrument creating the charge, or a copy, at its registered office while the charge remained in force"

-- src:11412 | (1A) An instrument creating any charge or a copy thereof, or a copy
-- src:11413 | of the series of debentures, as the case may be, that is required to be
-- src:11414 | kept under subsection (1) —
-- src:11416 | (a) is deemed to form part of the records that are required to be
-- src:11417 | kept under section 199(1); and
-- src:11419 | (b) for the purposes of section 199(2), must be retained by the
-- src:11420 | company for a period of 5 years after —
@ref s 138(1A)(a) (src:11412-11420)
GIVEN `the instrument, copy or series of debentures is one required to be kept under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(1A)(a) the instrument or copy is deemed to form part of the records required to be kept under section 199(1)` MEANS
    IF `the instrument, copy or series of debentures is one required to be kept under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is stated for an instrument or copy "that is required to be kept under subsection (1)"; it says nothing of any other

-- src:11419 | (b) for the purposes of section 199(2), must be retained by the
-- src:11420 | company for a period of 5 years after —
-- src:11425 | (i) the date the debt for which the charge was given was
-- src:11426 | paid or satisfied in whole;
-- src:11428 | (ii) the date the property or undertaking charged was
-- src:11429 | released or ceased to form part of the company’s
-- src:11430 | property or undertaking; or
-- src:11432 | (iii) where both of the events referred to in
-- src:11433 | sub‑paragraphs (i) and (ii) occur in any particular
-- src:11434 | case, the later of the dates.
@ref s 138(1A)(b) (src:11419-11434)
GIVEN `the debt for which the charge was given was paid or satisfied in whole` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the debt was paid or satisfied in whole` IS A DATE
      `the property or undertaking charged was released or ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the property or undertaking was released or ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 138(1A)(b) the last day of the period of 5 years for which the instrument must be retained` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the debt for which the charge was given was paid or satisfied in whole` AND `the property or undertaking charged was released or ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking`
        THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after`
                       (IF `the day the debt was paid or satisfied in whole` AT LEAST `the day the property or undertaking was released or ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking`
                        THEN `the day the debt was paid or satisfied in whole`
                        ELSE `the day the property or undertaking was released or ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking`)
                       5 Years)     -- (iii): "where both of the events ... occur ..., the later of the dates"
        IF `the debt for which the charge was given was paid or satisfied in whole`
        THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the debt was paid or satisfied in whole` 5 Years)     -- (i); fork F-K14
        IF `the property or undertaking charged was released or ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking`
        THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the property or undertaking was released or ceased to form part of the company's property or undertaking` 5 Years)     -- (ii); fork F-K14
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the 5 years run "after" an event of (i) or (ii); until one occurs the paragraph fixes no day

@ref s 138(1A)(b) (src:11419-11434)
GIVEN `the day asked` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the 5 years, if one is fixed` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(1A)(b) the instrument must still be retained on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day of the 5 years, if one is fixed`
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN (IF `the day asked` AT MOST lastDay
                            THEN JUST TRUE
                            ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a period of 5 years "after" the date; past its last day the paragraph requires no more retention (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): no event of (i) or (ii) has occurred, so the paragraph fixes no period

-- src:11438 | (2) Every company must keep at the registered office of the
-- src:11439 | company a register of charges and enter therein all charges
-- src:11440 | specifically affecting property of the company and all floating
-- src:11441 | charges on the undertaking or any property of the company, giving in
-- src:11442 | each case a short description of the property charged, the amount of
-- src:11443 | the charge and (except in the case of securities to bearer) the names of
-- src:11444 | the persons entitled thereto.
@ref s 138(2) (src:11438-11444)
GIVEN `the security is to bearer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 138(2) the particulars the company must give of each charge in its register of charges` MEANS
    IF `the security is to bearer`
    THEN LIST "a short description of the property charged",
              "the amount of the charge"
    ELSE LIST "a short description of the property charged",
              "the amount of the charge",
              "the names of the persons entitled to the charge"   -- "(except in the case of securities to bearer) the names of the persons entitled thereto"

@ref s 138(2) (src:11438-11444)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 134 act`
`s 138(2) the company must keep a register of charges at its registered office` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 138(2) keep a register of charges at the registered office`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 138(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not keep a register of charges at its registered office" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:11446 | (3) The instruments or copies thereof and the register of charges
-- src:11447 | kept pursuant to this section must be open to the inspection of any
-- src:11448 | creditor or member of the company without fee, and the register of
-- src:11449 | charges must also be open to the inspection of any other person on
-- src:11450 | payment of such fee not exceeding $2 for each inspection as is fixed
-- src:11451 | by the company.
@ref s 138(3) (src:11446-11451)
GIVEN `who asks` IS A `s 138(3) who asks to inspect`
      `what is to be inspected` IS A `s 138(3) what is to be inspected`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(3) the item must be open to the person's inspection` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who asks`
    WHEN `s 138(3) a creditor of the company` THEN JUST TRUE    -- "must be open to the inspection of any creditor or member of the company without fee"
    WHEN `s 138(3) a member of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 138(3) any other person` THEN
        CONSIDER `what is to be inspected`
        WHEN `s 138(3) the register of charges` THEN JUST TRUE    -- "the register of charges must also be open to the inspection of any other person on payment of such fee"
        WHEN `s 138(3) the instruments or copies kept under section 138` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the instruments or copies are made open to "any creditor or member"; for any other person only the register is mentioned

@ref s 138(3) (src:11446-11451)
GIVEN `who asks` IS A `s 138(3) who asks to inspect`
      `what is to be inspected` IS A `s 138(3) what is to be inspected`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 138(3) the most the company may charge for one inspection` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who asks`
    WHEN `s 138(3) a creditor of the company` THEN JUST 0    -- "without fee"
    WHEN `s 138(3) a member of the company` THEN JUST 0
    WHEN `s 138(3) any other person` THEN
        CONSIDER `what is to be inspected`
        WHEN `s 138(3) the register of charges` THEN JUST 2    -- "such fee not exceeding $2 for each inspection as is fixed by the company"
        WHEN `s 138(3) the instruments or copies kept under section 138` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection fixes no fee for another person's inspection of the instruments, because it does not open them to another person

@ref s 138(3) (src:11446-11451)
GIVEN `who asks` IS A `s 138(3) who asks to inspect`
      `what is to be inspected` IS A `s 138(3) what is to be inspected`
      `the fee the company has fixed for one inspection, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(3) the fee the company has fixed is within the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 138(3) the most the company may charge for one inspection` `who asks` `what is to be inspected`
    WHEN JUST limit THEN (IF `the fee the company has fixed for one inspection, in Singapore dollars` AT MOST limit
                          THEN JUST TRUE
                          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without fee" for a creditor or member; "such fee not exceeding $2 for each inspection" for any other person inspecting the register
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): see the limit function

-- src:11453 | (3A) Any person may, on application to a company and on payment
-- src:11454 | of a fee, not exceeding $1 for every page or part thereof, be furnished
-- src:11455 | with a copy of any instrument or debenture kept by the company
-- src:11456 | pursuant to this section within 3 days of the person making the
-- src:11457 | application.
@ref s 138(3A) (src:11453-11457)
GIVEN `the person has applied to the company for a copy of an instrument or debenture kept by the company under section 138` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has paid the fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(3A) the person may be furnished with a copy of the instrument or debenture` MEANS
    IF `the person has applied to the company for a copy of an instrument or debenture kept by the company under section 138` AND `the person has paid the fee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the person may be furnished with a copy "on application to a company and on payment of a fee"; the subsection does not say that a person who has not applied or paid may not (fork F-K15, split site (ii): "on application", not "where", "when" or "upon")

@ref s 138(3A) (src:11453-11457)
GIVEN `the day the person applied` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 138(3A) the last day for furnishing the copy` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the person applied` 3 Days     -- "within 3 days of the person making the application"

@ref s 138(3A) (src:11453-11457)
GIVEN `the number of pages, or parts of a page, of the copy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 138(3A) the most the company may charge for the copy, in Singapore dollars` MEANS
    `the number of pages, or parts of a page, of the copy` TIMES 1     -- "not exceeding $1 for every page or part thereof"

@ref s 138(3A) (src:11453-11457)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 134 act`
`s 138(3A) the company must furnish the copy within 3 days of the application` MEANS   -- fork F-K34: a duty derived from the person's entitlement to "be furnished with a copy ... within 3 days"; the text names no one who must furnish, and the company is the only party the sentence mentions
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 138(3A) furnish the person with a copy of an instrument or debenture kept under section 138`
    WITHIN 3
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not furnish the copy within 3 days of the application"

-- src:11459 | (4) If default is made in complying with this section, the company
-- src:11460 | and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of
-- src:11461 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:11462 | $2,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 138(4) (src:11459-11462)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 138` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 138(4) the person is guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 138` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 138` AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): an element of the offence is unmet ("If default is made in complying with this section, the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence"); split site (i); fork F-K10

@ref s 138(4) (src:11459-11462)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 138` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 138(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 138` AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default, as section 408(3) uses the phrase`)
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 2000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a default penalty"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the penalty is fixed only for a person the subsection makes guilty
